        },
        {
          "operation": "GET /menu_native/dynamic/tv_settings/audio",
          "status": 500,
          "count": 1,
          "known": true,
          "reason": "`validate_ha_config()` (`can_connect_with_auth_check()`), which Home Assistant's config flow runs to accept a token, lists the audio settings. No capture holds the audio menu, so the check fails against the emulator; capturing this GET with a valid token closes it."
        },
        {
          "operation": "GET /menu_native/dynamic/tv_settings/audio/mute",
          "status": 500,
          "count": 1,
          "known": true,
          "reason": "`is_muted()` reads the mute item from the audio menu. No capture holds it; a capture of the item in both states closes it."
        },
        {
          "operation": "GET /menu_native/dynamic/tv_settings/audio/volume",
          "status": 500,
          "count": 1,
          "known": true,
          "reason": "`get_current_volume()` reads the volume slider from the audio menu. No capture holds it, so the emulator cannot report its simulated volume on this route; a capture of the item, with its HASHVAL and value, closes it."
        },
        {
          "operation": "GET /menu_native/dynamic/tv_settings/system/system_information/tv_information/serial_number",
          "status": 500,
          "count": 1,
          "known": true,
          "reason": "`get_unique_id()` and `get_serial_number()` read the serial number from the settings tree; Home Assistant keys its config entry on it. The D24f-J09 capture holds no settings-tree read beyond the two device routes, so the emulator answers the crash page every uncaptured route gets. A capture of this GET off the set closes it."
        },
        {
          "operation": "GET /menu_native/dynamic/tv_settings/system/system_information/tv_information/version",
          "status": 500,
          "count": 1,
          "known": true,
          "reason": "`get_version()` reads the firmware version from the settings tree rather than deviceinfo's API_VERSION. No capture holds this read; capturing it off the set closes the gap."
        },
        {
          "operation": "GET /menu_native/dynamic/tv_settings/system/system_information/uli_information/esn",
          "status": 500,
          "count": 1,
          "known": true,
          "reason": "`get_esn()` reads the ESN from the settings tree with the AUTH token. No capture holds this read; capturing it off the set closes the gap."
        },
        {
          "operation": "PUT /app/launch",
          "status": 500,
          "count": 2,
          "known": true,
          "reason": "`launch_app()` and `launch_app_config()` send the community-documented `{\"VALUE\": {APP_ID, NAME_SPACE, MESSAGE}}` envelope. Probing the D24f-J09 showed firmware 3.3.3 answers that shape with the 'Unhandled Exception' page and launches only with the tv_settings REQUEST/VALUE/HASHVAL envelope; the emulator reproduces that crash and logs it as unsupported. Nothing captured answers pyvizio's shape with a launch, so this stays a gap until a set that accepts it is captured or pyvizio adopts the newer envelope."
        },
        {
          "operation": "PUT /menu_native/dynamic/tv_settings/devices/current_input",
          "status": 500,
          "count": 1,
          "known": true,
          "reason": "`set_input()` reads current_input (captured) and then writes it with a REQUEST/VALUE/HASHVAL MODIFY. No live input switch is captured, so the emulator serves only the GET and answers the write with the crash page; a capture of a real input change closes it."
        }
      ],
